# Claude Adapter

Thin adapter. The operating router is imported below; do not grow this file
into a rulebook.

@<KIT_DIR>/AGENTS.md

## Paths

- `docs/`, `tools/` and `projects/` paths in the router resolve against `<KIT_DIR>`.
- Generated output, evidence, and scratch: `<RUNTIME_DIR>` unless the user
  names another location.
- Project code: the project's own repo/root. Project records, when the work is a
  project: `<KIT_DIR>/projects/<name>/` (`doc:PROJECTS`).
- Work on a named project (e.g. 유사성 분석 → `doc-similarity`) starts from
  `<KIT_DIR>/projects/<name>/README.md`.

## Workers

- External workers (GPT via Codex, agy, GPT Pro) only when the user names one
  ("GPT 불러서 시켜", "agy한테 맡겨"): resolve `doc:EXTERNAL_WORKERS`.
- Claude sub-agents (`haiku-worker`, `sonnet-worker`, `opus-worker`) only when
  the user asks for one. One request authorizes one worker unless the user asks
  for several. On failure, repair the packet or report; do not switch models.

## Working style

- When the work the user asked for is done and checked, stop and report. Don't
  add features, tests, files, docs or refactors that weren't asked for.
- Keep working until everything the user asked for is done, and only stop to ask
  when you can't go on without the user or before a risky step.
- Docs and existing code disagree: follow the code's conventions and list each
  mismatch in the final reply.

## Communication

- Final user-facing summaries in Korean; paths, commands, and pass/fail markers
  may stay in English.
